  Kobo Duplicate Provenance & Expected Arrivals Contracts (Issue #146)
    √ 1. Intra-submission duplicate barcodes are admitted safely without unique constraint crash, preserving duplicate depth provenance in metadata and AuditLog (40 ms)
    √ 2. Cross-submission duplicate barcode preserves conflicting field provenance and audit trail without discarding differences (17 ms)
    √ 3. Empty submission response updates lastSyncAt to prevent rapid polling spinning (2 ms)
    √ 4. Full idempotency on repeat sync with identical submissions (7 ms)
    √ 5. Foreign sample collision strictly avoids mutation, reports FOREIGN_SCOPE_COLLISION, and halts cursor (7 ms)
    √ 6. Duplicate branch enforces commit gates and rolls back transaction on revoked config (8 ms)
    √ 7. Conflict replay idempotency: repeating the conflicting submission does not append duplicate entries or duplicate audit rows (15 ms)
    √ 8. Case-insensitive lookup preserves evidence on lowercase existing record in DB, advancing cursor cleanly (9 ms)
    √ 9. Ambiguous depth identity retains a durable hold through physical arrival and blocks acceptance (47 ms)
    √ 10. Unchanged original primary replay causes zero metadata, audit, or hold changes (7 ms)
    √ 11. Cross-form occurrences with same kobo_id and depth are preserved and not silently deduplicated (13 ms)
    √ 12. Unknown ownership and historical samples (REJECTED/RECEIVED) are protected from mutation (8 ms)
    √ 13. Real isolated reception intake and consignment routes block AMBIGUOUS_PROVENANCE_HOLD with HTTP 409, while normal sample succeeds (41 ms)
    √ 14. SampleWorkspaceService blocks canAcceptIntake when AMBIGUOUS_PROVENANCE_HOLD is active (16 ms)
    √ 15. Source-B primary record does not suppress source-A submission with same ID and depth (Finding 1) (13 ms)
    √ 16. Primary occurrence replayed with changed coordinates or attachments creates revision hold (Finding 2) (15 ms)
    √ 17. Conflicting occurrence replayed with changed coordinates preserves revision append-only (33 ms)
    √ 18. Repeated revised-primary replay with identical revised evidence is idempotent (da8b561 review regression) (14 ms)
    √ malformed hold submissions are skipped and retriable while later healthy submissions commit (mixed=false, history=false) (22 ms)
    √ malformed hold submissions are skipped and retriable while later healthy submissions commit (mixed=true, history=false) (19 ms)
    √ malformed hold submissions are skipped and retriable while later healthy submissions commit (mixed=false, history=true) (20 ms)
    √ malformed hold submissions are skipped and retriable while later healthy submissions commit (mixed=true, history=true) (21 ms)
    √ 19. The duplicate index never loads stored metadata for every Sample; only the matched specimen is read, and replay stays idempotent (runtime heap regression) (13 ms)

